{"strongs": "H5014", "word": "נָבַב", "translit": "na.vav", "root": "נבב", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "hollow out", "definition": "[ נָבַב ] verb hollow out (compare Assyrian imbubu , flute , Dl HWB 443 , Late Hebrew אַבּוּב id. , Aramaic אַבּוּבָא id. ; hence also Arabic knots in reed, part of reed between knots, reed ; see Hoffm LCB 1882, 321 Frä 23 Fl in Levy TW i. 417 ); — Qal Passive participle נָבוּב Job 11:12 ; Jer 52:21 נְבוּב Exod 27:8 ; Exod 38:7 — hollowed, hollow: of altar of tabernacle נְבוּב לֻחוֺת Exod 27:8 ; Exod 38:7 ( P ); of pillar in temple Jer 52:21 figurative אִישׁ נָבוּב Job 11:12 , i.e. empty, hollow-minded man. נֹ֫בֶה see נֹב .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4932')\">BDB4932</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5014')\">H5014</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4931')\">BDB4931</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4933')\">BDB4933</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>נָבַב</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>hollow out</highlightword> (compare Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>imbubu</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>flute</highlight>, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>HWB 443</sup></lookup>, Late Hebrew <bdbheb>אַבּוּב</bdbheb> <highlight>id.</highlight>, Aramaic <placeholder3142/> <bdbheb>אַבּוּבָא</bdbheb> <highlight>id.</highlight>; hence also Arabic <placeholder3143/> <highlight>knots</highlight> in reed, <highlight>part of</highlight> reed <highlight>between knots, reed</highlight>; see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hoffm')\">Hoffm<sup>LCB 1882, 321</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Frä')\">Frä<sup>23</sup></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Fl')\">Fl</lookup> in <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Levy')\">Levy<sup>TW i. 417</sup></lookup>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Passive participle</highlight> <bdbheb>נָבוּב</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 11:12\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(18,11,12)\">Job 11:12</